From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Shenk <kevin@avu.nu>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:18:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] Talk to the connection through
 WP_SQLite_Connection_Interface

The driver, the configurator, the information schema builder and
reconstructor, and the user-defined functions no longer reach for the PDO
handle: transactions, savepoints, attributes, the server version and
function registration go through the interface, and a "sqlite_connection"
driver option (or the WP_SQLite_Driver constructor) accepts any
implementation. The PHP < 8.4 inTransaction() polyfill goes: the connection
reports its own state. get_sqlite_pdo() still works for the local
connection and explains itself for the others.

Candidate for upstreaming as is.
